{"raw": {"https://stcatherine.peopleadmin.com/postings/11201": {"title": "Asst Prof of Social Work", "description": "St. Catherine Employment Site | Asst Prof of Social Work Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help St. Catherine University Home Page Benefits Strategic Plan Asst Prof of Social Work Bookmark this Hiring Approval Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Asst Prof of Social Work Division Academic Affairs Department/Office Social Work Master's Position Summary Information Advertisement The Social Work Department at St. Catherine University invites applications for a full-time Assistant Professor of Social Work position. The Assistant Professor will be a full-time, licensed, faculty member with experience in clinical social work to teach required MSW practice courses and other courses (as needed) in our MSW program. This is a 9-month position that teaches the equivalent of six courses annually. Responsibilities include: Teach graduate level social work courses, including both foundation and clinical level courses. Potential to teach in the BSW program (as needed). Engaged scholarly agenda and/or professional practice with activity in the Department of SW, HSSHS , the University and/or the social work profession. Engage in service to the Social Work Department, the MSW Program, the HSSHS , the University and the social work profession by participation/leadership in standing/ad hoc committees, and/or other service opportunities. St. Catherine University in St. Paul, Minnesota, is a comprehensive Catholic university and home to one of the nation\u2019s largest colleges for women, with associate and graduate programs for all genders. Founded by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet in 1905, the University integrates liberal arts and professional education within the Catholic traditions of intellectual inquiry and social teaching. Committed to excellence and opportunity, St. Catherine enrolls students in certificate, associate, baccalaureate, master\u2019s and doctoral programs in traditional day and evening/weekend/online formats. Minimum Qualifications Two years post MSW practice experience, and some experience teaching social work courses. Graduate license (or immediate eligibility for graduate license) in social work, State of Minnesota. Preferred Qualifications Independent Licensure eligibility ( LISW or LICSW ), 2 or more years teaching experience, clinical practice experience, critical self-reflective pedagogy, anti-oppressive practice experience, and experience teaching/mentoring diverse student populations. We will consider potential for a tenure-track position for candidates with a PhD. EEO Statement Compensation: Annual wage is $54,333 \u2013 $60,369 depending on qualifications and experience. The salary range listed reflects a good-faith estimate of what we reasonably anticipate to pay for this position, based on market data and internal equity, at the time of posting. Actual compensation will be determined based on qualifications, experience, skills, and other relevant factors. St. Catherine reserves the right to modify or adjust compensation depending on University needs. Benefits: Employees at St. Kate\u2019s feel a deep connection to the University\u2019s Mission and Vision, and they live their values at work. Benefits available to full-time employees include: Fourteen (14) paid holidays and paid \u201cgift\u201d days when the University is closed. Free tuition for employees and reduced tuition for their families after one year of service Health, dental, and vision insurance 403b retirement plan access Accrued sick time Specific information on all of our available benefits for full-time employees can be found HERE . St. Catherine University is an equal opportunity employer. Our commitment to inclusion reflects the central value of the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet to \u201clove of neighbor without distinction\u201d and provides a learning and working environment that is enriched by the diversity of all our members. Individuals of religious, racial, ethnic, gender identity, nation of origin, or disability groups that have traditionally had less representation in higher education are encouraged to apply. Should you need an interview accommodation please contact us at hr@stkate.edu or 651-690-6565. Application instructions for FACULTY Visit St. Kate Careers to apply. Three references and successful completion of a background check will be required for employment. St. Catherine University 2004 Randolph Avenue, St. Paul, MN 55105 Equal Opportunity Employer / Drug Free Workplace / Tobacco Free Workplace Our university is a proud member of the Upper Midwest HERC and is committed to recruiting and retaining outstanding and diverse faculty and staff and assisting dual career couples. For more information and to find other higher education jobs in the Upper Midwest region, visit: www.uppermidwestherc.org. Posting Detail Information Posting Number 20220381-FAC Posting Start Date 10/14/2026 Application Deadline 11/01/2026 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest level of completed education? Some high school High school diploma or GED Some college Associate's degree Bachelor's degree Some graduate school Master's degree ABD Professional degree (e.g., JD, MD) Doctoral degree * Are you presently legally authorized to work in the United States for any U.S. employer? Please be aware that St. Catherine University is only able to consider candidates who are authorized to work in the United States. Yes No * St. Catherine University welcomes applications from candidates who are traditionally under-represented. We are happy to consider candidates who are currently in possession of a temporary work visa, however, please be aware that we do not offer employment visa sponsorship. Will you now or in the future require an employer to sponsor you for an employment-based visa/status in the U.S. (e.g. H-1B status)? Yes No Maybe * Can you perform the essential functions of this position with or without accommodation? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Resume or Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Interests Statement of Teaching Philosophy Professional Reference Contact Information Personal statement on DEI in teaching Optional Documents 2004 Randolph Avenue St. Paul, MN 55105 800-945-4599 651-690-6000 Human Resources Derham Hall 113 651-690-6565 hr@stkate.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://stcatherine.peopleadmin.com/postings/11194": {"title": "Asst Prof of Nursing", "description": "St. Catherine Employment Site | Asst Prof of Nursing Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help St. Catherine University Home Page Benefits Strategic Plan Asst Prof of Nursing Bookmark this Hiring Approval Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Asst Prof of Nursing Division Academic Affairs Department/Office Nursing BA/BS Position Summary Information Advertisement The Nursing BA/BS Program at St. Catherine University invites applications for a full-time (0.75 FTE ) Assistant Professor of Nursing position. The School of Nursing is vibrant and dynamic, and our faculty educate students to develop the knowledge, technical skills, and professionalism they will need to be compassionate and successful nurses and leaders. Our nursing programs and curricula are delivered in an environment that embraces multicultural and social justice perspectives, relationships, interdisciplinary collaboration, and the liberal arts. The faculty member will teaches theory and clinical practice to BSN students and serves on committees to achieve the goals of the department, school and university.\u2019 Responsibilities: Facilitates student learning in assigned courses by teaching and advising a diverse student population, modeling socialization to nursing roles, and referring students to appropriate University services. Evaluates student learning in assigned courses. Assesses, designs, teaches, and evaluates curricular content and learning experiences in assigned courses to promote student learning outcomes. Maintains curricular integrity by ensuring course content promotes achievement of course student learning outcomes identified in the Program of study curriculum map. Selects methods and tools to assess, measure, and evaluate student learning outcomes in assigned courses. Uses identified assessment methods to evaluate achievement of student learning outcomes in assigned courses. Provides clear, timely, and specific evaluative feedback to students about course assignments and/or clinical performance. Participates in and/or completes the faculty course evaluation form at the end of the course. Integrates evaluative findings in the course improvement process. Evaluates adequacy of clinical placements for student learning in assigned courses. Participates in recruitment, orientation, and advising activities according to Program of Study, School of Nursing, and University requirements. Participates in designated committee, program, and School of Nursing activities to implement the program-specific systematic evaluation plan. Uses assessment and evaluative data from the program-specific systematic evaluation plan to promote achievement of student learning outcomes and program outcomes. St. Catherine University in St. Paul, Minnesota, is a comprehensive Catholic university and home to one of the nation\u2019s largest colleges for women, with associate and graduate programs for all genders. Founded by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet in 1905, the University integrates liberal arts and professional education within the Catholic traditions of intellectual inquiry and social teaching. Committed to excellence and opportunity, St. Catherine enrolls students in certificate, associate, baccalaureate, master\u2019s and doctoral programs in traditional day and evening/weekend/online formats. Minimum Qualifications Unencumbered licensure as registered nurse with current registration in Minnesota Master\u2019s degree in nursing Preferred Qualifications We seek creative, adaptable staff who enjoy working in a university climate that promotes multicultural understanding and cultural fluency, consistent with the University\u2019s mission and values. EEO Statement Compensation: Annual wage is $51,547 \u2013 $55,584 depending on qualifications and experience. The salary range listed reflects a good-faith estimate of what we reasonably anticipate to pay for this position, based on market data and internal equity, at the time of posting. Actual compensation will be determined based on qualifications, experience, skills, and other relevant factors. St. Catherine reserves the right to modify or adjust compensation depending on University needs. This is a full-time ( 0.75 FTE ) position. Employees working .50 \u2013 1.0 FTE are eligible to accrue sick time prorated based on their FTE status if less than a 1.0 FTE . Employees at St. Kate\u2019s feel a deep connection to the University\u2019s Mission and Vision, and they live their values at work. Benefits available to full-time employees include: Fourteen (14) paid holidays and paid \u201cgift\u201d days when the University is closed. Free tuition for employees and reduced tuition for their families after one year of service Health, dental, and vision insurance 403b retirement plan access Accrued sick time Paid parental leave after one year of service Specific information on all of our available benefits for full-time employees can be found HERE . St. Catherine University is an equal opportunity employer. Our commitment to inclusion reflects the central value of the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet to \u201clove of neighbor without distinction\u201d and provides a learning and working environment that is enriched by the diversity of all our members. Individuals of religious, racial, ethnic, gender identity, nation of origin, or disability groups that have traditionally had less representation in higher education are encouraged to apply. Should you need an interview accommodation please contact us at hr@stkate.edu or 651-690-6565. Application instructions for FACULTY Visit St. Kate Careers to apply. Three references and successful completion of a background check will be required for employment. St. Catherine University 2004 Randolph Avenue, St. Paul, MN 55105 Equal Opportunity Employer / Drug Free Workplace / Tobacco Free Workplace Our university is a proud member of the Upper Midwest HERC and is committed to recruiting and retaining outstanding and diverse faculty and staff and assisting dual career couples. For more information and to find other higher education jobs in the Upper Midwest region, visit: www.uppermidwestherc.org. Posting Detail Information Posting Number 20220380-FAC Posting Start Date 10/12/2026 Application Deadline 11/08/2026 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest level of completed education? Some high school High school diploma or GED Some college Associate's degree Bachelor's degree Some graduate school Master's degree ABD Professional degree (e.g., JD, MD) Doctoral degree * Are you presently legally authorized to work in the United States for any U.S. employer? Please be aware that St. Catherine University is only able to consider candidates who are authorized to work in the United States. Yes No * St. Catherine University welcomes applications from candidates who are traditionally under-represented. We are happy to consider candidates who are currently in possession of a temporary work visa, however, please be aware that we do not offer employment visa sponsorship. Will you now or in the future require an employer to sponsor you for an employment-based visa/status in the U.S. (e.g. H-1B status)? Yes No Maybe * Can you perform the essential functions of this position with or without accommodation? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Resume or Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents 2004 Randolph Avenue St. Paul, MN 55105 800-945-4599 651-690-6000 Human Resources Derham Hall 113 651-690-6565 hr@stkate.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://stcatherine.peopleadmin.com/postings/11163": {"title": "Adjunct Faculty - Prelicensure Nursing Programs", "description": "St. Catherine Employment Site | Adjunct Faculty - Prelicensure Nursing Programs Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help St. Catherine University Home Page Benefits Strategic Plan Adjunct Faculty - Prelicensure Nursing Programs Bookmark this Hiring Approval Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Adjunct Faculty - Prelicensure Nursing Programs Division Academic Affairs Department/Office Nursing BA/BS Position Summary Information Advertisement The School of Nursing at St. Catherine University invites applications for adjunct nursing faculty. St. Catherine University nursing faculty educate students to develop the knowledge, technical skills, and professionalism they will need to be compassionate and successful nurses and leaders. Our nursing programs and curricula are delivered in an environment that embraces diversity, social justice, interprofessional education, and the liberal arts. Our baccalaureate programs integrate holistic nursing and are endorsed by the American Holistic Nurses Credentialing Corporation. Our MSN : Entry-Level program prepares entry-level nurses (RNs) to become certified nurse leaders (CNLs). We hire ahead of each academic term. February-March applicants for Summer and/or Fall Term August applicants for Spring Term You may review our academic calendar here . Responsibilities may include: Didactic (classroom) instruction Clinical teaching and supervision Simulation or lab teaching All faculty: Monitor and assess student-learning outcomes and provide timely feedback to students on academic performance. Collaborate with faculty to deliver high-quality instruction. Clinical adjunct faculty must meet compliance requirements, including: Tdap MMR (or demonstrated immunity) Hepatitis B Varicella (or demonstrated immunity) Annual TB test Annual Influenza CPR for healthcare provider *requirements subject to change St. Catherine University in St. Paul, Minnesota, is a comprehensive Catholic university and home to one of the nation\u2019s largest colleges for women, with associate and graduate programs for all genders. Founded by the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet in 1905, the University integrates liberal arts and professional education within the Catholic traditions of intellectual inquiry and social teaching. Committed to excellence and opportunity, St. Catherine enrolls students in certificate, associate, baccalaureate, master\u2019s and doctoral programs in traditional day and evening/weekend/online formats. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree in Nursing for clinical instruction opportunities. Licensed and unencumbered registered nurse in the State of Minnesota. Two years of direct or indirect practice experience in an area of specialization. Preferred Qualifications Graduate degree in Nursing Teaching experience EEO Statement Compensation: $5,150 per course load (varies based on teaching assignment) The salary range listed reflects a good-faith estimate of what we reasonably anticipate paying for this position, based on market data and internal equity, at the time of posting. Actual compensation will be determined based on qualifications, experience, skills, and other relevant factors. St. Catherine reserves the right to modify or adjust compensation depending on University needs. Salary Examples: Teaching 12 clinical shifts (inclusive of grading, onboarding, etc.): $5665 Teaching 8 clinical shifts (inclusive of grading, onboarding, etc.): $4120 St. Catherine University is an equal opportunity employer. Our commitment to inclusion reflects the central value of the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet to \u201clove of neighbor without distinction\u201d and provides a learning and working environment that is enriched by the diversity of all our members. Individuals of religious, racial, ethnic, gender identity, nation of origin, or disability groups that have traditionally had less representation in higher education are encouraged to apply. Should you need an interview accommodation please contact us at hr@stkate.edu or 651-690-6565. Application instructions for FACULTY Visit St. Kate Careers to apply. Three references and successful completion of a background check will be required for employment. St. Catherine University 2004 Randolph Avenue, St. Paul, MN 55105 Equal Opportunity Employer / Drug Free Workplace / Tobacco Free Workplace Our university is a proud member of the Upper Midwest HERC and is committed to recruiting and retaining outstanding and diverse faculty and staff and assisting dual career couples. For more information and to find other higher education jobs in the Upper Midwest region, visit: www.uppermidwestherc.org. Posting Detail Information Posting Number 20220364-FAC Posting Start Date 09/24/2026 Application Deadline 10/25/2026 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Can you perform the essential functions of this position with or without accommodation? Yes No * St. Catherine University welcomes applications from candidates who are traditionally under-represented. We are happy to consider candidates who are currently in possession of a temporary work visa, however, please be aware that we do not offer employment visa sponsorship. Will you now or in the future require an employer to sponsor you for an employment-based visa/status in the U.S. (e.g. H-1B status)? Yes No Maybe * What is your highest level of completed education? Some high school High school diploma or GED Some college Associate's degree Bachelor's degree Some graduate school Master's degree ABD Professional degree (e.g., JD, MD) Doctoral degree * Are you presently legally authorized to work in the United States for any U.S. employer? Please be aware that St. Catherine University is only able to consider candidates who are authorized to work in the United States. Yes No * Select areas of past or current clinical practice where you would be comfortable teaching (select all that apply): Adult med/surg OB/Maternal Health Pediatrics Intensive Care Mental Health Community Health Long Term Care * What types of opportunities are you interested in? (select all that apply) Clinical teaching Lab teaching Simulation teaching Classroom teaching * Which schedules are you open to teaching? (select all that apply) Days Evenings Weekends Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume or Curriculum Vitae Professional Reference Contact Information Optional Documents 2004 Randolph Avenue St. Paul, MN 55105 800-945-4599 651-690-6000 Human Resources Derham Hall 113 651-690-6565 hr@stkate.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://stcatherine.peopleadmin.com/postings/11156": {"title": "Assistant Professor in Exercise &amp; Sport Science", "description": "St. Catherine Employment Site | Assistant Professor in Exercise &amp; Sport Science Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help St. Catherine University Home Page Benefits Strategic Plan Assistant Professor in Exercise & Sport Science Bookmark this Hiring Approval Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Assistant Professor in Exercise & Sport Science Division Academic Affairs Department/Office Exercise & Sport Science Position Summary Information Advertisement The Exercise & Sport Science Program at St. Catherine University invites applications for a full-time Assistant Professor in Exercise & Sport Science position. The Assistant Professor in Exercise & Sport Science will: Teach the equivalent of 1.0 FTE each academic year Advise EXSS students as assigned Develops and maintains a line of scholarship, where annual peer-reviewed dissemination is expected (presentations and/or publications) Collaborate and mentor undergraduate EXSS students with research Serve on departmental, HSSH , and/or university-elected committees Perform service (reviews, editorial boards, membership and service with national organizations) within the field of expertise Minimum Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in Exercise and Sport Science or related field Knowledge and expertise, and ability to teach courses, in the following areas: exercise physiology, exercise testing and prescription, strength and conditioning, introduction to exercise and sport science, exercise and sport science capstone. Prior experience developing and teaching labs in exercise physiology, exercise testing and prescription, and strength and conditioning Preferred Qualifications Doctoral or terminal professional degree in Exercise and Sport Science or related field Experience advising undergraduate students and helping them to plan and prepare for graduate programs in the health sciences. Prior training and mentorship in research and some scholarly expertise, allowing for the development of a successful line of scholarship. Experience using community-engaged learning practices in teaching. Expertise in some area of women\u2019s health Scholarship and teaching philosophy align with our university\u2019s social justice, women-centered mission EEO Statement Compensation: Annual wage is $74,477 \u2013 $82,752 depending on qualifications and experience. The salary range listed reflects a good-faith estimate of what we reasonably anticipate to pay for this position, based on market data and internal equity, at the time of posting. Actual compensation will be determined based on qualifications, experience, skills, and other relevant factors. St. Catherine reserves the right to modify or adjust compensation depending on University needs. Benefits: Employees at St. Kate\u2019s feel a deep connection to the University\u2019s Mission and Vision, and they live their values at work. Benefits available to full-time employees include: Fourteen (14) paid holidays and paid \u201cgift\u201d days when the University is closed. Free tuition for employees and reduced tuition for their families after one year of service Health, dental, and vision insurance 403b retirement plan access Accrued sick time Specific information on all of our available benefits for full-time employees can be found HERE . St. Catherine University is an equal opportunity employer. Our commitment to inclusion reflects the central value of the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet to \u201clove of neighbor without distinction\u201d and provides a learning and working environment that is enriched by the diversity of all our members. Individuals of religious, racial, ethnic, gender identity, nation of origin, or disability groups that have traditionally had less representation in higher education are encouraged to apply. Should you need an interview accommodation please contact us at hr@stkate.edu or 651-690-6565. Application instructions for FACULTY Visit St. Kate Careers to apply. Three references and successful completion of a background check will be required for employment. St. Catherine University 2004 Randolph Avenue, St. Paul, MN 55105 Equal Opportunity Employer / Drug Free Workplace / Tobacco Free Workplace Our university is a proud member of the Upper Midwest HERC and is committed to recruiting and retaining outstanding and diverse faculty and staff and assisting dual career couples. For more information and to find other higher education jobs in the Upper Midwest region, visit: www.uppermidwestherc.org. Posting Detail Information Posting Number 20220378-FAC Posting Start Date 09/09/2026 Application Deadline 10/16/2026 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest level of completed education? Some high school High school diploma or GED Some college Associate's degree Bachelor's degree Some graduate school Master's degree ABD Professional degree (e.g., JD, MD) Doctoral degree * Are you presently legally authorized to work in the United States for any U.S. employer? Please be aware that St. Catherine University is only able to consider candidates who are authorized to work in the United States. Yes No * St. Catherine University welcomes applications from candidates who are traditionally under-represented. We are happy to consider candidates who are currently in possession of a temporary work visa, however, please be aware that we do not offer employment visa sponsorship. Will you now or in the future require an employer to sponsor you for an employment-based visa/status in the U.S. (e.g. H-1B status)? Yes No Maybe * Can you perform the essential functions of this position with or without accommodation? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Interests Statement of Teaching Philosophy Professional Reference Contact Information Statement of Research Interest Optional Documents Copies of papers, articles, scholarly or creative work or service activities 2004 Randolph Avenue St. Paul, MN 55105 800-945-4599 651-690-6000 Human Resources Derham Hall 113 651-690-6565 hr@stkate.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://stcatherine.peopleadmin.com/postings/11144": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Nursing, BSN College for Adults (Hybrid/Evening/Weekend)", "description": "St. Catherine Employment Site | Assistant Professor of Nursing, BSN College for Adults (Hybrid/Evening/Weekend) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help St. Catherine University Home Page Benefits Strategic Plan Assistant Professor of Nursing, BSN College for Adults (Hybrid/Evening/Weekend) Bookmark this Hiring Approval Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Assistant Professor of Nursing, BSN College for Adults (Hybrid/Evening/Weekend) Division Academic Affairs Department/Office Nursing- BSN Position Summary Information Advertisement The Nursing- BSN Program at St. Catherine University invites applications for a full-time Assistant Professor of Nursing, BSN College for Adults (Hybrid/Evening/Weekend) position. The faculty member is accountable for student learning in the School of Nursing (SoN) by fulfilling responsibilities that contribute to the achievement of student learning and program outcomes. These responsibilities are congruent with St. Catherine University and School of Nursing policies for faculty assessment and evaluation. This position involves teaching theory and clinicals to BSN students. It will also include advising and committee work. Duties will include: Facilitates student learning in assigned courses by teaching and advising a diverse student population, modeling socialization to nursing roles, and referring students to appropriate University services. Evaluates student learning in assigned courses. Assesses, designs, teaches, and evaluates curricular content and learning experiences in assigned courses to promote student learning outcomes. Maintains curricular integrity by ensuring course content promotes achievement of course student learning outcomes identified in the Program of study curriculum map. Selects methods and tools to assess, measure, and evaluate student learning outcomes in assigned courses. Uses identified assessment methods to evaluate achievement of student learning outcomes in assigned courses. Provides clear, timely, and specific evaluative feedback to students about course assignments and/or clinical performance. Participates in and/or completes the faculty course evaluation form at the end of the course. Integrates evaluative findings in the course improvement process. Evaluates adequacy of clinical placements for student learning in assigned courses. Facilitates student learning in assigned courses by teaching and advising a diverse student population, modeling socialization to nursing roles, and referring students to appropriate University services. Participates in recruitment, orientation, and advising activities according to POS , DoN, and University requirements. Evaluates the adequacy of POS , nursing program, DoN, University, and community resources that are used to promote student achievement of learning outcomes in assigned courses. Identifies resources needed to promote student achievement of learning outcomes in assigned courses and communicates rationale for needed resources to the Program Director. Participates in recruitment, orientation, and advising activities according to Program of Study, School of Nursing, and University requirements. Communicates accurate information about the DoN nursing programs to students, faculty and professional colleagues, and other external audiences. Engages in activities that promote positive relationships with students, faculty and professional colleagues, clinical and community agencies, alumnae, and other external groups. Serves on Program of Study, School of Nursing, and/or University committees. Participates in designated committee, program, and School of Nursing activities to implement the program-specific systematic evaluation plan. Uses assessment and evaluative data from the program-specific systematic evaluation plan to promote achievement of student learning outcomes and program outcomes. Collaborates with nursing faculty, Program Director, Associate Dean of Nursing, and Dean of Nursing to establish and accomplish short- and long-range goals for the nursing program. Models and mentors relational presence that is rooted in Catholic Social Teaching and consistent with the mission and values of St. Catherine University and the School of Nursing vision, mission, and philosophy. Engages in scholarship activities that develop expertise and ability to fulfill faculty responsibilities. Contributes to professional development of faculty colleagues through peer review, mentoring, consultation, and scholarship activities. Minimum Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in Nursing Current and unencumbered licensure as registered nurse in Minnesota Preferred Qualifications Doctoral degree in nursing EEO Statement Compensation: Annual wage is $68,730 \u2013 $74,500 depending on qualifications and experience. The salary range listed reflects a good-faith estimate of what we reasonably anticipate to pay for this position, based on market data and internal equity, at the time of posting. Actual compensation will be determined based on qualifications, experience, skills, and other relevant factors. St. Catherine reserves the right to modify or adjust compensation depending on University needs. Benefits: Employees at St. Kate\u2019s feel a deep connection to the University\u2019s Mission and Vision, and they live their values at work. Benefits available to full-time employees include: Fourteen (14) paid holidays and paid \u201cgift\u201d days when the University is closed. Free tuition for employees and reduced tuition for their families after one year of service Health, dental, and vision insurance 403b retirement plan access Accrued sick time Specific information on all of our available benefits for full-time employees can be found HERE . St. Catherine University is an equal opportunity employer. Our commitment to inclusion reflects the central value of the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet to \u201clove of neighbor without distinction\u201d and provides a learning and working environment that is enriched by the diversity of all our members. Individuals of religious, racial, ethnic, gender identity, nation of origin, or disability groups that have traditionally had less representation in higher education are encouraged to apply. Should you need an interview accommodation please contact us at hr@stkate.edu or 651-690-6565. Application instructions for FACULTY Visit St. Kate Careers to apply. Three references and successful completion of a background check will be required for employment. St. Catherine University 2004 Randolph Avenue, St. Paul, MN 55105 Equal Opportunity Employer / Drug Free Workplace / Tobacco Free Workplace Our university is a proud member of the Upper Midwest HERC and is committed to recruiting and retaining outstanding and diverse faculty and staff and assisting dual career couples. For more information and to find other higher education jobs in the Upper Midwest region, visit: www.uppermidwestherc.org. Posting Detail Information Posting Number 20220377-FAC Posting Start Date 09/11/2026 Application Deadline 10/19/2026 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest level of completed education? Some high school High school diploma or GED Some college Associate's degree Bachelor's degree Some graduate school Master's degree ABD Professional degree (e.g., JD, MD) Doctoral degree * Are you presently legally authorized to work in the United States for any U.S. employer? Please be aware that St. Catherine University is only able to consider candidates who are authorized to work in the United States. Yes No * St. Catherine University welcomes applications from candidates who are traditionally under-represented. We are happy to consider candidates who are currently in possession of a temporary work visa, however, please be aware that we do not offer employment visa sponsorship. Will you now or in the future require an employer to sponsor you for an employment-based visa/status in the U.S. (e.g. H-1B status)? Yes No Maybe * Can you perform the essential functions of this position with or without accommodation? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume or Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Interests Professional Reference Contact Information Optional Documents Other Document 1 2004 Randolph Avenue St. Paul, MN 55105 800-945-4599 651-690-6000 Human Resources Derham Hall 113 651-690-6565 hr@stkate.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://stcatherine.peopleadmin.com/postings/11012": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor - Sonography - Echocardiography", "description": "St. Catherine Employment Site | Adjunct Instructor - Sonography - Echocardiography Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help St. Catherine University Home Page Benefits Strategic Plan Adjunct Instructor - Sonography - Echocardiography Bookmark this Hiring Approval Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Adjunct Instructor - Sonography - Echocardiography Division Academic Affairs Department/Office Sonography Position Summary Information Advertisement The Sonography Department at St. Catherine University invites applications for an Adjunct Instructor in Sonography \u2013 Echocardiography. The Adjunct Instructor will: Teach courses, as needed, in the Sonography curriculum. Provide career and additional mentorship to students Strengthen the preparation of future sonographers Provide feedback to the program director(s) on needed improvements and strengths of courses and student preparation The Sonography department is part of the Henrietta Schmoll School of Health Sciences ( HSSHS ). The Sonography Department at St. Catherine University is one of only two universities in the Upper Midwest to offer a Bachelor of Science degree in sonography. St. Catherine University specializes in educating health care professionals and has an outstanding reputation in the healthcare community as the metro area\u2019s leading healthcare educator. The Sonography Program also has an extensive clinical network where students will gain training in real-world environments. Join our team of dedicated faculty who share their personal insight into the profession! With 19 degree programs and approximately 100 faculty, the HSSHS is the largest of St. Kate\u2019s three schools. Degrees are offered to students at all levels, from the associate to the doctoral level. The school is distinguished by programs\u2019 shared focus on ecological approaches to health, intercultural competency, and interprofessional collaboration. The Institute of Simulation and Interprofessional Learning (I- SAIL ) provides resources and expertise to support the development and implementation of high-impact educational activities within HSSHS and the School of Nursing. Potential courses available to teach include: - SON1620 Cardiac Anatomy and Physiology - SON 1630 Foundations of Echocardiography - SON 1642 Echo Foundations Scan Lab - SON 2015 Ultrasound Physics and Instrumentation - SON 2100 Adult Echo - SON 2122 Adult Echo Scan Lab - SON 2455 Congenital Heart Disease - SON 2460 Concepts in Echocardiography - SON 2510 Adult Echo II - SON 2710 Adult Echo III - SON 3360 Comprehensive Review Lab - SON 4010 Capstone Project - SON 4020 Seminar in Advanced Echo Imaging Applicants are asked to identify courses of interest in their cover letter. The Sonography Department will review applications as they are received. Applicants need to apply by August 7th for consideration to teach fall courses and by December 1st for consideration to teach spring courses. Minimum Qualifications Associate\u2019s degree Active sonography credential in Echocardiography Preferred Qualifications Previous teaching experience Currently practicing in the field Bachelor\u2019s degree or higher EEO Statement Compensation: $5,150 per course The salary range listed reflects a good-faith estimate of what we reasonably anticipate to pay for this position, based on market data and internal equity, at the time of posting. Actual compensation will be determined based on qualifications, experience, skills, and other relevant factors. St. Catherine reserves the right to modify or adjust compensation depending on University needs. St. Catherine University is an equal opportunity employer. Our commitment to inclusion reflects the central value of the Sisters of St. Joseph of Carondelet to \u201clove of neighbor without distinction\u201d and provides a learning and working environment that is enriched by the diversity of all our members. Individuals of religious, racial, ethnic, gender identity, nation of origin, or disability groups that have traditionally had less representation in higher education are encouraged to apply. Should you need an interview accommodation please contact us at hr@stkate.edu or 651-690-6565. Application instructions for FACULTY Visit St. Kate Careers to apply. Three references and successful completion of a background check will be required for employment. St. Catherine University 2004 Randolph Avenue, St. Paul, MN 55105 Equal Opportunity Employer / Drug Free Workplace / Tobacco Free Workplace Our university is a proud member of the Upper Midwest HERC and is committed to recruiting and retaining outstanding and diverse faculty and staff and assisting dual career couples. For more information and to find other higher education jobs in the Upper Midwest region, visit: www.uppermidwestherc.org. Posting Detail Information Posting Number 20220371-FAC Posting Start Date 07/24/2026 Application Deadline 05/05/2027 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is your highest level of completed education? Some high school High school diploma or GED Some college Associate's degree Bachelor's degree Some graduate school Master's degree ABD Professional degree (e.g., JD, MD) Doctoral degree * Are you presently legally authorized to work in the United States for any U.S. employer? Please be aware that St. Catherine University is only able to consider candidates who are authorized to work in the United States. Yes No * St. Catherine University welcomes applications from candidates who are traditionally under-represented. We are happy to consider candidates who are currently in possession of a temporary work visa, however, please be aware that we do not offer employment visa sponsorship. Will you now or in the future require an employer to sponsor you for an employment-based visa/status in the U.S. (e.g. H-1B status)? Yes No Maybe * Can you perform the essential functions of this position with or without accommodation? Yes No Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents 2004 Randolph Avenue St. Paul, MN 55105 800-945-4599 651-690-6000 Human Resources Derham Hall 113 651-690-6565 hr@stkate.edu To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://stcatherine.peopleadmin.com/postings/11011": {"title": "Adjunct Instructor - Sonography - Abdomen - Extended, Obstetrics &amp; Gynecology", "description": "St. Catherine Employment Site | Adjunct Instructor - Sonography - Abdomen - Extended, Obstetrics &amp; Gynecology Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help St. Catherine University 