phy Program also has an extensive clinical network where students will gain training in real-world environments. Join our team of dedicated faculty who share their personal insight into the profession! With 19 degree programs and approximately 100 faculty, the HSSHS is the largest of St. Kate\u2019s three schools. Degrees are offered to students at all levels, from the associate to the doctoral level. The school is distinguished by programs\u2019 shared focus on ecological approaches to health, intercultural competency, and interprofessional collaboration. The Institute of Simulation and Interprofessional Learning (I- SAIL ) provides resources and expertise to support the development and implementation of high-impact educational activities within HSSHS and the School of Nursing. Potential courses available to teach include: - SON1605 Abdomen I - SON 1615 Abdominal I Lab - SON 1705 Reproductive Systems in Sonography - SON 1715 Reproductive Systems Skills Lab - SON 1805 Abdomen II - SON 1815 Abdominal II Lab - SON 2015 Ultrasound Physics and Instrumentation - SON 2205 Obstetrical-Neonatal Sonography - SON 2210 Obstetrical/Neonatal Skills Lab - SON 2305 Elements of Vascular Sonography - SON 2310 Elements of Vascular Sonography Skills Lab - SON 3305 Small Parts - SON 3310 Small Parts Lab - SON 4010 Capstone Project Applicants are asked to identify courses of interest in their cover letter. The Sonography Department will review applications as they are received. Applicants need to apply by August 7th for consideration to teach fall courses and by December 1st for consideration to teach spring courses. Minimum Qualifications Associate\u2019s Degree Active sonography credential in Abdomen- Extended, Obstetrics & Gynecology Proficiency in using sonography equipment for lab and hands-on components Preferred Qualifications Previous teaching experience Currently practicing in the field Bachelor\u2019s degree or higher EEO Statement Compensation: $5,150 per course The salary ra